1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:06,021
As I said earlier, there is I think at Rexford an excellent combination of physical

2
00:00:06,021 --> 00:00:10,520
and geographical advantages, as well as having a rural setting

3
00:00:10,520 --> 00:00:12,443
and still being close to central London,

4
00:00:12,443 --> 00:00:20,070
something that will certainly be of interest to you is that Rexford is just 35 minutes from London Airport.

5
00:00:20,070 --> 00:00:24,550
At Rexford we have a strong research capability.

6
00:00:24,550 --> 00:00:31,080
We came 7th out of 101 universities in last year's research assessment

7
00:00:31,120 --> 00:00:33,662
carried out by a government body

8
00:00:33,662 --> 00:00:39,230
and did particularly well in your particular subjects, engineering and science.

9
00:00:39,230 --> 00:00:46,880
Actually we got a top research grade of five for engineering, geography and computer sciences.

10
00:00:46,880 --> 00:00:57,500
One further point, and I know from talking to you individually that a number of you may be looking for some experience in industry after the course

11
00:00:58,260 --> 00:01:00,220
Is that all our science

12
00:01:00,220 --> 00:01:06,000
and engineering research departments have unusually close relationships with industry in the area.

13
00:01:06,000 --> 00:01:09,420
Anyway that's enough sales talk from me

14
00:01:09,780 --> 00:01:12,469
I'll just take a sip of this coffee that's just arrived,

15
00:01:12,469 --> 00:01:17,500
thank you, and then I'll say something about what actually happens when you apply.

16
00:01:17,500 --> 00:01:24,585
Right... Now if you do decide to make an application,

17
00:01:24,625 --> 00:01:28,780
what you do is send it directly to me in my department

18
00:01:28,780 --> 00:01:34,170
I will then immediately send confirmation and the application process begins.

19
00:01:34,170 --> 00:01:38,026
Er... I'd like to say at this point that you shouldn't worry

20
00:01:38,066 --> 00:01:40,660
if this process doesn't work all that quickly

21
00:01:41,060 --> 00:01:44,472
I mean occasionally there are postal problems

22
00:01:44,472 --> 00:01:50,020
but most often the hold-up is caused by references. The people you give as referees,

23
00:01:50,020 --> 00:01:53,190
shall we say, take their time to reply.

24
00:01:53,190 --> 00:01:58,000
Anyway, it's absolutely normal for this process to take three to four months.

25
00:01:58,000 --> 00:02:01,820
What I do in this period is keep in touch with you

26
00:02:01,820 --> 00:02:04,480
and reassure you that things are moving along.

27
00:02:04,480 --> 00:02:11,513
One of the ways we've devised to help you decide about applying as well as later when you've been accepted,

28
00:02:11,513 --> 00:02:14,326
hopefully, is to put you in contact with,

29
00:02:14,326 --> 00:02:19,600
if possible, a student from your own country who is at present studying with us.

30
00:02:19,600 --> 00:02:23,220
What you can do is phone them up. We will, of course

31
00:02:23,220 --> 00:02:27,170
liaise between you, and discuss your concerns with them.

32
00:02:27,170 --> 00:02:33,387
That way you can get an objective opinion of what you can expect if you come to live

33
00:02:33,387 --> 00:02:36,150
and study at Rexford. Not only the academic atmosphere

34
00:02:36,150 --> 00:02:39,604
but important details like what the leisure facilities are like

35
00:02:39,604 --> 00:02:44,440
and whether the English weather and food are really as awful as everybody says!

36
00:02:44,440 --> 00:02:46,955
If you decide you can face it,

37
00:02:46,955 --> 00:02:51,640
the contact can also help you just before you leave

38
00:02:51,640 --> 00:02:54,500
with tips on what to pack and that sort of thing.

39
00:02:54,500 --> 00:02:58,080
At the moment I think we've got two second-year students

40
00:02:58,080 --> 00:03:01,000
and one postgraduate from this country.

41
00:03:01,000 --> 00:03:05,270
Now to move on to the other concerns you expressed earlier.

42
00:03:05,270 --> 00:03:08,980
At a UK university, as I'm sure you know

43
00:03:09,300 --> 00:03:12,377
You will be in an environment where independent learning is the norm,

44
00:03:12,377 --> 00:03:15,743
which takes most students a while to adjust to,

45
00:03:15,743 --> 00:03:20,720
and at a time when you will be separated from your normal surroundings

46
00:03:20,800 --> 00:03:22,850
and, in most cases, your family.

47
00:03:22,850 --> 00:03:24,940
This can be a difficult time.

48
00:03:24,940 --> 00:03:31,097
But remember that something like 25% of our student body are international students like yourselves,

49
00:03:31,097 --> 00:03:34,791
and that there are several organisations in the university

50
00:03:34,791 --> 00:03:39,000
and city whose main purpose is to offer help

51
00:03:39,000 --> 00:03:43,000
and ensure that your time with us is enjoyable and useful.

52
00:03:43,000 --> 00:03:47,550
One or two of you touched on the subject of accommodation earlier.

53
00:03:47,550 --> 00:03:50,790
So I'll just add a few points:

54
00:03:50,790 --> 00:03:58,659
it is the University's policy to give priority in the allocation of residence places to three categories,

55
00:03:58,659 --> 00:04:03,750
and those are: visiting students, exchange students and new postgraduate students.

56
00:04:03,750 --> 00:04:11,102
However, demand exceeds supply, so there is still a need to put your name down early for campus accommodation,

57
00:04:11,102 --> 00:04:13,810
particularly if your family is accompanying you.

58
00:04:13,810 --> 00:04:19,155
This means that the earlier you decide whether you want to study with us...

59
00:04:19,155 --> 00:04:24,500
and so get the procedure moving, the better it will be for everybody. Yes.

60
00:04:24,500 --> 00:04:28,640
What if you would prefer to live outside the university?

61
00:04:28,640 --> 00:04:33,370
If you're planning to live off-campus, you've got to sort things out even earlier.

62
00:04:33,370 --> 00:04:35,528
As with everything in short supply,

63
00:04:35,528 --> 00:04:41,103
the good accommodation gets snapped up months before the beginning of term-in other words

64
00:04:41,544 --> 00:04:42,980
if you're starting in October

65
00:04:43,400 --> 00:04:47,760
you need to be thinking about it in June or at the very latest July

66
00:04:47,760 --> 00:04:52,580
So you do need to think very carefully about what you need

67
00:04:52,760 --> 00:04:56,130
how much you can afford to pay, well in advance.

68
00:04:56,130 --> 00:05:01,600
What you can't do is leave it until a few days before the start of term.

69
00:05:01,600 --> 00:05:04,480
The agencies in town are pretty good

70
00:05:04,840 --> 00:05:07,550
It's just a matter of contacting them in good time.

71
00:05:07,550 --> 00:05:12,950
Of course, we have a full-time accommodation officer available to help all students.

72
00:05:12,950 --> 00:05:15,620
She'll get in touch with you when you're accepted

73
00:05:16,200 --> 00:05:18,211
She's got plenty of contacts in the town

74
00:05:18,211 --> 00:05:21,170
and will deal with the agencies on your behalf.

75
00:05:21,170 --> 00:05:26,140
One or two of you asked me earlier about your level of spoken English.

76
00:05:26,140 --> 00:05:29,680
Obviously most of you have already achieved a lot

77
00:05:29,680 --> 00:05:32,475
I wish I could speak your language half as well.

78
00:05:32,475 --> 00:05:40,570
Having said that though, I'm afraid the lecturers will make little or no allowance for the presence of non-native speakers in the audience.

79
00:05:40,570 --> 00:05:49,759
So anything you can do to improve your spoken English-even beyond the pretty high levels most of you have already reached. Will help make your stay

80
00:05:49,759 --> 00:05:52,700
with us that bit more fun for you.

81
00:05:52,700 --> 00:05:56,757
Some extra practice before you arrive is worth more than,

82
00:05:56,757 --> 00:06:01,220
for example private lessons afterwards, when you won't really have time.

83
00:06:01,220 --> 00:06:07,000
Oh... and one last thing before I invite further questions: it's very important that you...
